research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dini-needs-a-continuous-limit.log-6-BOUNDARY: The endpoint \(x=1\) is correctly handled: \(\chi\) is discontinuous there because the required \(\delta\) fails for \(\varepsilon=1\), using only domain points. The constant sequences at \(x=0\) and \(x=1\) preserve pointwise monotonicity. No degenerate, empty, or zero cases affect the counterexample.
