research/audit/wave12-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-13434-          "source_section": "Statement refuted",
research/audit/wave12-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-13435-          "quote": "**Refuted claim:** pointwise convergence of real-valued functions on a closed bounded interval implies uniform convergence. For $k\\in\\mathbb{N}$ define $f_k:[0,1]\\to\\mathbb{R}$ by $$f_k(x):=x^{k+1}.$$ Then $(f_k)$ converges pointwise to the endpoint indicator $$\\chi(x):=\\begin{cases}0,&0\\le x<1,\\\\1,&x=1,\\end{cases}$$ but the convergence is not uniform.",
research/audit/wave12-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-13436-          "quote_selection": "full-source-section",
